al and alternative medicine</article-title><source>Emerg Med Clin North Am</source><year>2000</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>709</fpage><lpage>722</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0733-8627(05)70154-1</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11130934</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="other">Chen JK CT: Chinese Medical Herbology and Pharmacology. 2001.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Takeuchi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Homma</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Inoue</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kato</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Murata</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Ogasawara</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Case of intractable ventricula fibrillation by a multicomponent dietary supplement containing ephedra and caffeine overdose</article-title><source>Chudoku Kenkyu</source><year>2007</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>269</fpage><lpage>271</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17784561</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><label>12.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dwyer</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Allison</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Coates</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dietary supplements in weight reduction</article-title><source>J Am Diet Assoc</source><year>2005</year><volume>105</volume><fpage>S80</fpage><lpage>86</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jada.2005.02.028</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15867902</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boumba</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitselou</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Vougiouklakis</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fatal poisoning from ingestion of Datura stramonium seeds</article-title><source>Vet Hum Toxicol</source><year>2004</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>82</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15080209</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lord</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Tagore</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Gower</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Pusey</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nephropathy caused by Chinese herbs in the UK</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1999</year><volume>354</volume><fpage>481</fpage><lpage>482</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(99)03380-2</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10465175</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bent</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ko</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Commonly used herbal medicines in the United States: a review</article-title><source>Am J Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>116</volume><fpage>478</fpage><lpage>485</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.amjmed.2003.10.036</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15047038</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>WF</given-names></name><name><surname>Wen</surname><given-names>KC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hsiao</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Adulteration by synthetic therapeutic substances of traditional Chinese medicines in Taiwan</article-title><source>J Clin Pharmacol</source><year>1997</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>344</fpage><lpage>350</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9115061</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR17"><label>17.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yee</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Chu</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>YM</given-names></name><name><surname>Choo</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Regulatory control of Chinese Proprietary Medicines in Singapore</article-title><source>Health Policy</source><year>2005</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>149</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.healthpol.2003.09.013</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15607377</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR18"><label>18.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tay</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Seah</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Arsenic poisoning from anti-asthmatic herbal preparations</article-title><source>Med J Aust</source><year>1975</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>424</fpage><lpage>428</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1186550</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR19"><label>19.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ernst</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Adulteration of Chinese herbal medicines with synthetic drugs: a sys